WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.063 --> 00:00:02.570
- Here's a little story
sure to make you smile.

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:04.225
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:04.225 --> 00:00:05.499
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.499 --> 00:00:07.030
(audience cheers)

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:10.020
After a wedding, couples
usually like to look back

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:11.890
at the video of their big day.

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:13.460
Sadly for 14 years,

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:14.870
Drew and Kayla from Oregon couldn't.

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:17.755
That's because when they went
to put their tape on DVD,

00:00:17.755 --> 00:00:22.755
they were told it was blank,
which is so sad, and funny.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.070
Years later, Drew got a call
from a friend who it turns out,

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:29.590
had found the wedding
footage at the church.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:31.160
Instead of just telling his wife,

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.570
Drew decided to unveil it
for her in like a big way.

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:37.680
So on their anniversary, he
rented out the local theater.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.410
Kayla thought he was gonna
show her their favorite movie.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.590
And then this happened.

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:43.870
I love that she hadn't seen it.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.860
He surprised her with
rolling their wedding day

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.190
on the silver screen.

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:50.822
And we have the couple
on the line right now.

00:00:50.822 --> 00:00:51.655
(audience clapping)

00:00:51.655 --> 00:00:54.700
Who're watching our partner
station KMTR in Eugene.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:56.514
So hey Kayla, hey Drew.

00:00:56.514 --> 00:00:58.264
(audience cheers)

00:00:58.264 --> 00:00:59.181
- Hi Kelly.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.780
- I mean, first of all
Drew this is so romantic.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:03.830
That's so sweet.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.710
She did well by picking you.

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:07.730
And it must've been heartbreaking though,

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:10.260
to find out that you had
lost your wedding footage.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:13.130
Like how heartbreaking
was that in the moment?

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:13.963
- I mean,

00:01:13.963 --> 00:01:14.970
I knew we still had our pictures

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:16.590
and we'd be able to look back on those,

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.110
but there's something
about having the video,

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:19.900
which just gives you that extra layer

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:21.120
of seeing people in action

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:22.953
and hearing the noises and remembering it.

00:01:22.953 --> 00:01:27.350
And when I got that call,
that my friend had found them,

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:28.550
I was just overjoyed.

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:30.943
He didn't even know that we
didn't have them at the time,

00:01:30.943 --> 00:01:33.920
but I knew I had to plan
some kind of big surprise

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.220
cause she was just gonna be ecstatic.

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:37.053
- Oh, that's so cool.

00:01:37.053 --> 00:01:40.450
How emotional was that
moment in the theater Kayla?

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:43.910
- Oh my gosh. I was so overwhelmed.

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:45.430
I could not believe that we were watching

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:46.263
our wedding videos.

00:01:46.263 --> 00:01:47.240
Like I thought,

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.150
how about knew was our
wedding videos and thought,

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:50.790
how on earth does he have these?

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:52.570
Like how are we watching these right now?

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:55.840
But it is just so special
to like see all the people.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:57.870
Like the guy who married us is super funny

00:01:57.870 --> 00:02:00.050
and I remember laughing
and having a good time,

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:02.506
but couldn't quite
remember what he had said.

00:02:02.506 --> 00:02:04.259
So its so fun to just remember

00:02:04.259 --> 00:02:06.640
everything that really happened that day.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.220
- And now I've told
her it's for next year.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:10.600
It's her turn to try and top this.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:12.360
I am done for next year.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.193
- There's no way.

00:02:13.193 --> 00:02:15.010
He's so good at surprises.

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:17.080
I can't top this.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:18.500
- Oh my God. Well, that's so cool.

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:20.410
And also you spend so
much money on that day.

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:22.190
It's good to have it on film.

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:24.070
It's like weddings are expensive.

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:25.249
- For sure.

00:02:25.249 --> 00:02:27.260
- Thank you so much Drew and Kayla.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:28.710
I'm liking your posts right now.

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:30.471
- [Kayla] Thank you so much.
- [Drew] Thank you.

00:02:30.471 --> 00:02:33.760
- That's not all y'all our
season long partner Pilot Pen

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:35.131
the go-to pen at the
Kelly Clarkson show thinks

00:02:35.131 --> 00:02:37.440
that your story is as sweet as we do.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:38.810
So in recognition,

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:40.520
there'll be using their
frixion erasable pen

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:42.380
to write you a check for a $1000.

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:43.230
How's that sound?

00:02:45.684 --> 00:02:46.708
- [Drew] Thank you so much.

00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:48.890
- And also happy anniversary.

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:49.930
That's amazing.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.353
14 years it's amazing
you guys keep it going.

